adjudication.rationale:
The diff does add `sendAddGuestsEmails` in `packages/emails/email-manager.ts` that branches per attendee:
```ts
if (newGuests.includes(attendee.email)) {
  return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeScheduledEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
} else {
  return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeAddGuestsEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
}
```
However, the proposed finding is an architectural/design critique (template “coupling”) rather than a verifiable defect (bug/security/correctness issue) introduced by the diff. Nothing in the diff shows this branching is incorrect or causes misbehavior; it appears intentional to send different email content to newly added guests vs existing attendees. Therefore it’s not a “real problem” in the strict sense requested.
